"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project involves implementing AI algorithms to potentially increase efficiency by 20%. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, both achieved ahead of schedule. The team has been expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. A budget of $2M has been approved to cover research, development, and marketing. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. The project is moving into the development phase under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming meetings scheduled for August 5th, August 1st (budget discussion), and September 10th (onboarding). A celebration for the testing milestone is planned for October 10th."
